# Docker does NOT read .gitignore. Without this file, the `COPY . .` of the
# Dockerfile bakes into the image everything .gitignore was protecting — first
# among them `.env`, whose ENVIRONMENT=local turns off authentication entirely
# (api/deps.py serves every unauthenticated request as the seeded dev user, and
# main.py gives that account role="admin"). Second, `uploads/`: the clients'
# CCTP corpus, readable by anyone who can pull the image.
#
# Found by the /audit:security authz surface on 2026-09-03.

# Secrets. The single most important line in this file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.*

# Client corpus — confidential, never published (CLAUDE.md, Protected Files)
uploads/

# Local environments and caches: useless in the image, and they carry
# absolute paths from the build machine.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
*.egg-info/

# Tests and tooling do not ship: the image runs the app, it does not test it.
tests/
